IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: W.P. (Crl.) No. 1770 of 2019
CITATION: (2019) 9 SCC 24
YEAR: 2019

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: R. Banumathi, A.S. Bopanna, Hrishikesh Roy

PARTIES:
P. Chidambaram vs Enforcement Directorate

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002, Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 45 PMLA, Section 439 CrPC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
triple test, flight risk, tampering of evidence, witness influence

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Emphasized that bail considerations turn on the triple test: whether the accused is a flight risk, likely to tamper with evidence, or likely to influence witnesses.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 45 PMLA, Section 439 CrPC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

